From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] App permissions: the folder offer and the command-line review

ADR-052 step 3 (design-center 8bd4ccf, mockups/app-perms/offer.html).
org.projectluma.AppPermissions1 emits Refused(app, folder) once per app and
folder when an app was refused one of the person's folders. The Shell offers
it with its standard notification banner (lumaPermissionOffer.js), never a
dialog and never pausing the app: the app's own source (its name the source
line, its icon the tile), the Settings icon as a badge only the Shell can
set (lumaShellBadge), "Music folder", "Let Tide use your Music folder?",
Allow and Not now of equal weight. The answer goes back with AnswerOffer;
dismissing counts as Not now. On a TV, where the lip is hidden, the same
banner at x1.5 at the top right with the remote's focus on Not now.

ReviewRequested(app, name), raised after a command-line install that went
ahead at the suggested level, becomes a standard notification from Valet,
"Kiln installed", whose Review runs `luma-install --review APP`.

lumaPermissionOffer.showOffer() is the one offer surface; the layer
permission offer can draw through it too.
---
